course: dictionary
lesson: 14955
title: Learning again: relearn
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Relearn is made of two parts. Re- means again, and learn means to get knowledge or a skill. So to relearn something is to learn it again.
explain: You relearn something when you have forgotten it or lost it. «After the summer holidays, we had to relearn our times tables.» The times tables were not new. They had slipped out of memory.
explain: You can also relearn a new or better way of doing something you already did. «After her accident, Maya had to relearn how to walk.» She could walk before, but now she learns it again, with help.
fact: Relearn is a verb. Its forms are relearn, relearns, relearned or relearnt, and relearning.
fact: «Relearn» means to learn something again that you have forgotten or lost.
fact: «Relearn» can also mean to learn a new or better way of doing something you already did.
fact: The phrases «relearn how to» and «have to relearn» are often used with it.
fact: Re- at the start of a word often means again.
exercise: «After the holidays, Leo had to relearn his spellings.» What does relearn mean here? | *Learn again the spellings he had forgotten | Learn a language he has never heard before | Forget his spellings for ever | Write his spellings on the board
exercise: The prefix re- in relearn means what? | Away from | *Again | Very | Before
exercise: «Maya had to relearn how to walk.» Why does she need to relearn? | She was learning to fly | Her shoes were new | She wanted to run faster than ever | *Her accident made her lose the skill
test: «Sam had forgotten the dance steps, so he had to relearn them before the show.» What does relearn mean here? | Watch other people dance | Make up brand new dance steps | Skip the show | *Learn again the steps he had forgotten
test: «Priya learned a better way to hold her pencil, so she had to relearn how to write.» What is she doing? | Forgetting how to write | Buying a new pencil | Drawing a picture | *Learning a better way of doing something she already did
exam: Which sentence best shows someone relearning? | «Ben read the book for the first time.» | *«Ben had forgotten the poem, so he had to relearn it.» | «Ben ate his lunch quickly.»
